   "text": "The drawing is a 1,4-diene-3-one steroid (ring A on the right) with 9-fluoro, 11-hydroxy, 17-hydroxy, a 17-hydroxyacetyl side chain (C(=O)CH2OH), and methyl groups at C10, C13 and C16.\n\nThe ring system is drawn mirror-flipped relative to the usual steroid layout (ring A on the right, ring D on the left). That reverses the usual wedge/hash reading, so I read the stereochemistry in the flipped frame:\n\n- The C13 and C10 methyls are hashed, which corresponds to \u03b2.\n- 17-OH, 9-F and the C16 methyl are wedged, which corresponds to \u03b1.\n- 11-OH and 8-H are hashed (\u03b2), and 14-H is wedged (\u03b1).\n\nA 16\u03b1-methyl with 9\u03b1-fluoro and 11\u03b2-hydroxy is the pattern of dexamethasone, not its 16\u03b2 epimer betamethasone. I wrote the SMILES from this assignment, matching it to the known dexamethasone stereochemistry rather than deriving each centre's @/@@ from scratch.\n\nSMILES: C[C@@H]1C[C@H]2[C@@H]3CCC4=CC(=O)C=C[C@@]4([C@]3([C@H](C[C@@]2([C@]1(C(=O)CO)O)C)O)F)C"
